# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0041 (Manage secrets)
# cilium-operator requires secret access for Gateway API TLS certificates and IPsec/WireGuard encryption keys
KSV-0041
AVD-KSV-0041

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0056 (Manage Kubernetes networking)
# cilium-operator manages cluster-wide network policies, services, endpoints, and Gateway API routing
KSV-0056
AVD-KSV-0056

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0109 (ConfigMap with secrets)
# False positive: cilium-config keys reference secret namespaces and taint keys (e.g. bgp-secrets-namespace) without containing actual credentials
KSV-0109
AVD-KSV-0109

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0005 (SYS_ADMIN capability added)
# cilium daemonset requires SYS_ADMIN to load eBPF programs, attach to cgroups, and manage network namespaces
KSV-0005
AVD-KSV-0005

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0009 (Access to host network)
# cilium agent, cilium-envoy, and cilium-operator require host network access to manage host interfaces, BGP peering, and localhost API communication
KSV-0009
AVD-KSV-0009

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014 (Root file system is not read-only)
# Cilium components write runtime sockets, compiled eBPF objects, runtime state, certificates, and web caches
KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0014

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0017 (Privileged)
# cleanCiliumState init container and Cilium agent require privileged access to initialize host interfaces and eBPF maps
KSV-0017
AVD-KSV-0017

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0024 (Access to host ports)
# cilium agent, cilium-envoy, and cilium-operator bind host ports for health checks, Prometheus metrics, and proxy listeners
KSV-0024
AVD-KSV-0024

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0119 (NET_RAW capability added)
# cilium agent requires NET_RAW for ARP/ICMP processing and BPF masquerading
KSV-0119
AVD-KSV-0119

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0121 (Kubernetes resource with disallowed volumes mounted)
# cilium daemonset requires hostPath volume mounts (/sys/fs/bpf, /sys/fs/cgroup, /var/run/cilium) for eBPF maps and cgroup management
KSV-0121
AVD-KSV-0121

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001 (Can elevate its own privileges)
# cilium agent and envoy require privilege escalation to manipulate kernel network devices and host routing tables
KSV-0001
AVD-KSV-0001

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012 (Runs as root user)
# Cilium CNI agent, envoy proxy, operator, and cert generation require root user to interact with kernel subsystems and host mounts
KSV-0012
AVD-KSV-0012

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0022 (Specific capabilities added)
# cilium agent and envoy require specific Linux capabilities (NET_ADMIN, SYS_ADMIN, etc.) for eBPF operations and network steering
KSV-0022
AVD-KSV-0022

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0023 (hostPath volumes mounted)
# cilium agent and envoy require hostPath mounts (/sys/fs/bpf, /var/run/cilium, etc.) to share eBPF maps and sockets with the host
KSV-0023
AVD-KSV-0023

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0025 (SELinux custom options set)
# cilium daemonset sets specific SELinux security options for host directory and socket access
KSV-0025
AVD-KSV-0025

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0037 (User resources should not be placed in kube-system namespace)
# Cilium is core cluster networking infrastructure and components appropriately reside in the kube-system namespace
KSV-0037
AVD-KSV-0037

